    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/AprilNEA/OpenLogi/releases</releaseNotes>
    <tags>openlogi logitech hidpp mouse keyboard remap options-plus</tags>
    <summary>A native, local-first alternative to Logitech Options+, written in Rust. Remap buttons, DPI, and SmartShift over HID++.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[OpenLogi is a native, local-first alternative to Logitech Options+, written in Rust. It talks to Logitech HID++ peripherals over Logi Bolt and Unifying receivers, Bluetooth-direct connections, or USB cables, without running Logi Options+.

Remap buttons, drive DPI and SmartShift, and switch profiles per app, without a Logitech account, telemetry, or the official Options+ install. Everything stays local: bindings live in a plain TOML file, and device changes are written straight to the device over HID++.

This package installs the current version of OpenLogi.
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
